WEBVTT

00:00:23.859 --> 00:00:27.080
[♪♪♪]

00:00:41.703 --> 00:00:44.967
Ginny...

00:00:51.104 --> 00:00:53.411
Ginny. Oh, Ginny,
please don't be dead.

00:00:53.411 --> 00:00:55.151
Wake up, wake up.

00:00:55.151 --> 00:00:57.589
Please wake up.

00:00:57.589 --> 00:00:59.155
She won't wake.

00:01:05.292 --> 00:01:08.121
Tom. Tom Riddle.

00:01:08.121 --> 00:01:09.949
What do you mean
she won't wake?

00:01:09.949 --> 00:01:11.690
She's not...?

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:13.518
She's still alive,
but only just.

00:01:13.518 --> 00:01:15.520
Are you a ghost?

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:19.306
A memory preserved in a diary
for 50 years.

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:23.267
She's cold as ice.

00:01:23.267 --> 00:01:27.314
Ginny, please don't be dead.
Wake up.

00:01:27.314 --> 00:01:29.969
You've got to help me, Tom.
There's a basilisk.

00:01:29.969 --> 00:01:31.405
It won't come
until it's called.

00:01:35.235 --> 00:01:36.454
Give me my wand, Tom.

00:01:36.454 --> 00:01:38.238
You won't be needing it.

00:01:38.238 --> 00:01:41.241
Listen, we've got to go.
We've got to save her.

00:01:41.241 --> 00:01:43.199
I'm afraid I can't
do that, Harry.

00:01:43.199 --> 00:01:45.724
You see, as poor
Ginny grows weaker,

00:01:45.724 --> 00:01:46.812
I grow stronger.

00:01:48.248 --> 00:01:49.293
Yes, Harry,

00:01:49.293 --> 00:01:50.598
it was Ginny Weasley

00:01:50.598 --> 00:01:53.166
who opened
the Chamber of Secrets.

00:01:53.166 --> 00:01:55.734
No. She couldn't.
She wouldn't.

00:01:55.734 --> 00:01:57.213
It was Ginny
who set the basilisk

00:01:57.213 --> 00:01:58.693
on the Mudbloods
and Filch's cat.

00:01:58.693 --> 00:01:59.999
Ginny who wrote

00:01:59.999 --> 00:02:01.174
the threatening messages
on the walls.

00:02:01.174 --> 00:02:02.436
But why?

00:02:02.436 --> 00:02:04.873
Because I told her to.

00:02:04.873 --> 00:02:07.876
You'll find
I can be very persuasive.

00:02:07.876 --> 00:02:09.835
Not that she knew
what she was doing.

00:02:09.835 --> 00:02:12.054
She was, shall we say,
in a kind of trance.

00:02:14.143 --> 00:02:16.320
Still, the power of the diary
began to scare her,

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.453
and she tried to dispose of it
in the girls' bathroom,

00:02:19.453 --> 00:02:23.936
and then,
who should find it but you?

00:02:23.936 --> 00:02:26.721
The very person
I was most anxious to meet.

00:02:26.721 --> 00:02:29.420
And why did you want
to meet me?

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:33.511
I knew I had to talk to you,
meet you if I could,

00:02:33.511 --> 00:02:35.121
so I decided
to show you my capture

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:36.601
of that brainless oaf, Hagrid,

00:02:36.601 --> 00:02:37.950
to gain your trust.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:41.301
Hagrid's my friend.

00:02:41.301 --> 00:02:42.694
And you framed him,
didn't you?

00:02:42.694 --> 00:02:45.261
It was my word against Hagrid's.

00:02:45.261 --> 00:02:47.829
Only Dumbledore
seemed to think he was innocent.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.877
I'll bet Dumbledore
saw right through you.

00:02:51.877 --> 00:02:53.400
He certainly kept

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.315
an annoyingly close watch
on me after that.

00:02:55.315 --> 00:02:57.448
I knew it wouldn't be safe
to open the Chamber again

00:02:57.448 --> 00:02:58.797
while I was still at school,

00:02:58.797 --> 00:03:00.755
so I decided
to leave behind a diary,

00:03:00.755 --> 00:03:03.236
preserving my 16-year-old self
in its pages,

00:03:03.236 --> 00:03:05.760
so that one day,
I would be able to lead another,

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:09.155
to finish Salazar Slytherin's
noble work.

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:11.113
Well, you haven't finished it
this time.

00:03:11.113 --> 00:03:12.332
In a few hours,

00:03:12.332 --> 00:03:14.465
the Mandrake draught
will be ready,

00:03:14.465 --> 00:03:16.945
and everyone who was Petrified
will be all right again.

00:03:16.945 --> 00:03:19.208
Haven't I told you?

00:03:19.208 --> 00:03:23.082
Killing Mudbloods
doesn't matter to me anymore.

00:03:23.082 --> 00:03:27.521
For many months now,
my new target has been you.

00:03:29.349 --> 00:03:30.698
How is it that a baby

00:03:30.698 --> 00:03:32.744
with no extraordinary
magical talent

00:03:32.744 --> 00:03:35.573
was able to defeat
the greatest wizard of all time?

00:03:35.573 --> 00:03:40.055
How did you escape
with nothing but a scar

00:03:40.055 --> 00:03:41.753
while Lord Voldemort's powers
were destroyed?

00:03:41.753 --> 00:03:43.276
Why do you care how I escaped?

00:03:43.276 --> 00:03:45.974
Voldemort was after your time.

00:03:45.974 --> 00:03:51.980
Voldemort is my past,
present and future.

